From 491143e2d95a6d04f2232b043fd104167a2ec389 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: well0nez <8986239+well0nez@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 19:02:59 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 47/75] h713: hdmi: publish never walks past the CEA block

publish() followed the CEA-861 data blocks while i < 128 + DTD offset
and i < 255, but never checked a block's length against that end, nor
that the extension was a CEA block: a malformed upload (DTD offset 125,
a vendor block header at byte 252) wrote the physical-address byte up to
three bytes past the 256-byte stack buffer - into the saved r16 of
system_state_machine on the ResetEDIDModule path (PRUEFUNG5 F1, checked
in the disassembly).

The walk now needs tag 2 and a DTD offset of at least 4, ends at min(128
+ offset, 255), and stops at the first block that would run past it; the
byte written then always lies inside. Well-formed EDIDs publish as
before.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/hdmi/sun50i-h713-hdmi.c | 16 ++++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/hdmi/sun50i-h713-hdmi.c b/drivers/hdmi/sun50i-h713-hdmi.c
index 5b25b9e..ccd86b1 100644
--- a/drivers/hdmi/sun50i-h713-hdmi.c
+++ b/drivers/hdmi/sun50i-h713-hdmi.c
@@ -385,10 +385,22 @@ publish(void)
 		for (int i = 0; i < EDID_BLOCK; ++i)
 			blk[i] = src[i];
 		phys = sh_rd8(SH_PORTMAP + 8 * port + REC_PHYS);
-		/* CEA-861 data block collection: tag 3 with IEEE 00 0c 03. */
-		for (int i = 128 + 4; i < 128 + blk[128 + 2] && i < 255;) {
+		/*
+		 * CEA-861 data block collection: tag 3 with IEEE 00 0c 03. It
+		 * ends at the DTD offset (byte 2 of the extension, whose tag
+		 * is 2) and before the checksum; a block that runs past that
+		 * end is not followed, so a malformed upload never reaches
+		 * beyond blk[] (PRUEFUNG5 F1). With len >= 5 inside the end,
+		 * the byte written, i + 4, lies inside it too.
+		 */
+		int end = 128 + blk[128 + 2] < 255 ? 128 + blk[128 + 2] : 255;
+
+		for (int i = 128 + 4; blk[128] == 0x02 && blk[128 + 2] >= 4 &&
+		     i < end;) {
 			uint8_t tag = blk[i] >> 5, len = blk[i] & 0x1f;
 
+			if (i + 1 + len > end)
+				break;
 			if (tag == 3 && len >= 5 && blk[i + 1] == 0x03 &&
 			    blk[i + 2] == 0x0c && blk[i + 3] == 0x00)
 				blk[i + 4] = phys;
